@startuml config-lifecycle
title Config Lifecycle — Constructor Contract\ninit() ALWAYS yields a valid object

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #388E3C
skinparam DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3E0
skinparam DiamondBorderColor #EF6C00
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F5F5F5
skinparam NoteBorderColor #999

|#E8F5E9|this (kernel)|
|#FFF3E0|config (persistence)|
|#FCE4EC|env files (pure state)|

|this (kernel)|

start

partition "**this.init** — the constructor" {

  :private.this.resolve.fundamentals();
  note right
    BASH_SOURCE chain walker.
    Walk BASH_SOURCE[] from deepest frame.
    Find dir containing both ""this"" + ""config"" files.
    Symlink-safe: ""cd -P"" resolves real path.
    Sets: OOSH_DIR, CONFIG_PATH, OOSH_MODE.
    **Never guesses $HOME/oosh.**
  end note

  if (CONFIG set + user.env exists?) then (yes)
    :source $CONFIG (user.env);
    :source oosh.env (if exists);
    :source log.env (if exists);
    :resolve.fundamentals() again;
    note right: Override anything from\npolluted env files

    :private.this.selfheal();
    note right
      Scan user.env for pollution.
      If ANY non-pure-state line found
      → call **config.save** (harvest-resolve-merge).
      **Always RC=0.** Constructor never fails.
    end note

  else (no — fresh install)
    :source $CONFIG (if exists);
    :source oosh.env / log.env (if exist);
    :resolve.fundamentals() again;
    :private.this.selfheal();
  endif
}

note right
  **Constructor contract:**
  After this.init, the object IS valid.
  Fundamentals canonical. Pollution healed.
  No error path — always succeeds.
end note

|config (persistence)|

partition "**config.init** — in-memory constructor" {
  :resolve.fundamentals();
  :CONFIG_FILE = ""user.env"";
  :mkdir -p CONFIG_PATH;
  :CONFIG = CONFIG_PATH/CONFIG_FILE;
  note right: Sets variables in memory only.\nDoes NOT write files.
}

partition "**config.save** (no args) — persistent constructor\n**config.repair** = alias for this" {

  :=== PHASE 1: HARVEST ===;
  note right
    Read existing user.env **FILE**.
    Extract valid ""export VAR=value"" lines.
    Extract ""source *.env"" lines (Rule A).
    Skip all logic (: ${, $(, [ ], conditionals).
    **Then** add from live env (declare -px)
    — only vars NOT already harvested from file.
    → Preserves user state from any state:
      primed, born-broken, or corrupted.
  end note

  :=== PHASE 2: RESOLVE ===;
  :resolve.fundamentals();
  note right: OOSH_DIR/CONFIG_PATH/OOSH_MODE\nfrom BASH_SOURCE — always correct

  :=== PHASE 3: MERGE + WRITE ===;
  note right
    **Order in user.env:**
    1. Fundamentals (canonical, override stale)
    2. Harvested user vars (skip fundamentals)
    3. Source chain from harvest (Rule A)
  end note

  |env files (pure state)|
  :user.env ← write;
  note right
    ""export CONFIG_PATH=""/root/config""""
    ""export OOSH_DIR=""/root/oosh""""
    ""export OOSH_MODE=""dev""""
    ""export BASH_FILE=""/usr/bin/bash""""
    ""export PATH=""...""""
    ""export TRON_MONITOR_PANE=""...""""
    ""source $CONFIG_PATH/oosh.env""
    ""source $CONFIG_PATH/log.env""
  end note

  |config (persistence)|
  :config.save oosh OOSH;
  note right: Dump OOSH_* vars from\ndeclare -px → oosh.env

  |env files (pure state)|
  :oosh.env ← write;

  |config (persistence)|
  :config.save log LOG;

  |env files (pure state)|
  :log.env ← write;

  |config (persistence)|
  :config.validate();
  note right
    Scan user.env line-by-line.
    **ACCEPT**: export, declare, comment,
    blank, source *.env, bare VAR=
    **REJECT**: everything else
    (: ${, $(, [ ], { }, conditionals)
  end note

  if (violations == 0?) then (yes)
    :valid object;
  else (no)
    :error.log (but constructor\nnever fails — selfheal\nwill re-run on next boot);
  endif
}

|config (persistence)|

partition "**config.save <name> <PREFIX>**\n(per-module save)" {
  :Dump declare -px filtered by PREFIX;
  note right
    e.g. config.save oosh OOSH
    → writes all OOSH_* vars to oosh.env
    Only from live env (not file harvest).
    Used AFTER init primes the env.
  end note

  |env files (pure state)|
  :name.env ← write;
}

|config (persistence)|

partition "**config.add <name>**\n(composition)" {
  :Append ""source $CONFIG_PATH/<name>.env""\nto user.env;
  :config.clean (sort -u dedup);
  note right
    Rule A: source *.env is valid in env files.
    Idempotency: sort -u deduplicates
    (but appending first means the file
    briefly has a duplicate — see GAP-1).
  end note
}

|this (kernel)|

partition "**Boot sequence** (.bashrc)" {
  :source ~/config/user.env;
  note right: Pure state — exports +\nsource chain loads oosh.env, log.env
  :source $OOSH_DIR/this;
  :this.init();
  note right: resolve.fundamentals +\nselfheal if polluted
}

stop

legend bottom left
  **File hierarchy (pure state only)**
  ├── ~/config/user.env     — fundamentals + user vars + source chain
  │   ├── source oosh.env   — OOSH_MODE, OOSH_PM, OOSH_SSH_CONFIG_HOST, ...
  │   ├── source log.env    — LOG_LEVEL, LOG_DEVICE, LOGNAME
  │   └── source custom.env — (any config.add additions)
  **All files**: export/declare + comments + blanks + source *.env ONLY
  **Constructor contract**: init always yields valid object, never fails
  **Repair = init**: config.repair() { config.save; }
endlegend

@enduml
